o control the model's behavior.\n\nThe core components of the pipeline involve:\n\n1. **Representation Reading**: The paper introduces Representation Reading via Linear Artificial Tomography (LAT), which has three steps: (1) design a stimulus+task that elicits a target concept/function; (2) collect hidden states at well-chosen token positions (often the last token or the concept token); (3) fit a simple linear model (usually PCA on paired differences) to obtain a reading vector for the concept/function.\n\n2. **Representation Control**: The paper includes three baselines and three operators for control: Controllers include (a) the reading vector (stimulus-independent), (b) a per-input contrast vector from paired prompts, and (c) LoRRA — Low-Rank Representation Adaptation, a LoRA-style adapter; Operators include linear combination (stimulation/suppression), piece-wise (conditional boost using sign), and projection (erase a component)."],"durationSeconds":7.7040674410000065}}
