{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DnF5iqQTGhantS9LHsa6bg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Figure 1 Visual Analysis\n\nFigure 1 illustrates the research methodology through a structured diagram showing how LLMs handle conflicting knowledge sources.\n\n## Visual Elements and Layout\n\nThe illustration presents a horizontal flow showing three main components:\n\n1. **Input Prompt Section**: Displays contradictory information where contextual knowledge (the false statement) precedes a query about the same subject-relation pair.\n\n2. **Model Processing**: The central area depicts model layers, showing how neural network activations are extracted during inference as the contradiction is processed.\n\n3. **Output Classification**: The rightmost section shows how extracted activations train a classifier to distinguish whether the model's response relied on parametric knowledge (learned during training) or contextual knowledge (provided in the prompt).\n\n## Design Features\n\nThe diagram uses a left-to-right progression to guide viewers through the experimental workflow. The layout emphasizes the sequential nature: presenting conflicting information, observing internal model states, then classifying knowledge source usage. The visual hierarchy helps readers understand that specific model activations correlate with knowledge source selection, enabling researchers to \"probe\" which knowledge the model ultimately prioritizes when facing contradictions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01ee3a65-b626-47fe-81be-aa3af5ee612a","uuid":"cd59728d-1a35-4536-9d8e-43d1ff2ee5be","timestamp":"2026-05-25T16:20:16.281Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":268214,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Figure 1 Visual Analysis\n\nFigure 1 illustrates the research methodology through a structured diagram showing how LLMs handle conflicting knowledge sources.\n\n## Visual Elements and Layout\n\nThe illustration presents a horizontal flow showing three main components:\n\n1. **Input Prompt Section**: Displays contradictory information where contextual knowledge (the false statement) precedes a query about the same subject-relation pair.\n\n2. **Model Processing**: The central area depicts model layers, showing how neural network activations are extracted during inference as the contradiction is processed.\n\n3. **Output Classification**: The rightmost section shows how extracted activations train a classifier to distinguish whether the model's response relied on parametric knowledge (learned during training) or contextual knowledge (provided in the prompt).\n\n## Design Features\n\nThe diagram uses a left-to-right progression to guide viewers through the experimental workflow. The layout emphasizes the sequential nature: presenting conflicting information, observing internal model states, then classifying knowledge source usage. The visual hierarchy helps readers understand that specific model activations correlate with knowledge source selection, enabling researchers to \"probe\" which knowledge the model ultimately prioritizes when facing contradictions.","durationMs":4779,"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2410.05817v1"}}
